+/-!
+# The dart→sector-point map and the arc→`PolyArc` bridge (Track A, GAP pieces)
+
+This file supplies the three concrete pieces the `EdmondsCompatible`
+instantiation in `EdmondsConstruction.lean` needs in order to take the abstract
+region family `dr` to be `regionAt ∘ dartSectorPoint`.
+
+The downstream consumer is `edmondsCompatibleAtPrefix`
+(`EdmondsConstruction.lean`), whose `hcomp` field requires, for every prefix
+dart `d`,
+`∃ p ∈ drawingComplementIn (G.prefixEdges m hm) R₀,`
+`  dr m hm d = regionAt (G.prefixEdges m hm) R₀ p`.
+With `dr m hm d := regionAt (G.prefixEdges m hm) R₀ (dartSectorPoint … d)` this is
+discharged by taking `p := dartSectorPoint … d` together with the membership
+`dartSectorPoint_mem_drawingComplementIn`.
+
+## Why not `regionAt ∘ dartAnchor`
+
+`dartAnchor d ∈ G.V` is a drawing **vertex**, i.e. an arc endpoint, hence it lies
+**in** `arcUnion` and is therefore **not** in `drawingComplementIn = R₀ ∖ arcUnion`.
+So `regionAt … (dartAnchor d) = connectedComponentIn (R₀ ∖ arcUnion) (anchor) = ∅`
+— degenerate.  `dartSectorPoint` fixes this by moving **off** the vertex into a
+small angular wedge that misses the arc union (the design `vertexPlus a v b ∩
+ball v ε`), where `v` is the dart's anchor vertex.
+
+## What is proved here, and what is a flagged geometric obligation
+
+* `straightPolyArc` (deliverable 3) and `arcToPolyArc` — turning a straight
+  graph arc into a one-segment `PolyArc` — are proved **sorry-free**: the two
+  no-self-crossing fields are vacuous at `numSegs = 1`, and `distinct` reduces to
+  the endpoints being distinct.
+* `dartSectorPoint` (deliverable 1) is built by `Classical.choose` from a single
+  named existence obligation `exists_dartSectorPoint`, and
+  `dartSectorPoint_mem_drawingComplementIn` (deliverable 2) is then
+  `Classical.choose_spec` — **sorry-free given the obligation**.
+* `exists_dartSectorPoint` is the one genuine plane-geometry fact that is **not
+  yet in the codebase**: that a small angular wedge at a drawing vertex avoids the
+  (finite) arc union.  It is isolated as a single `private` lemma with body
+  `sorry`, flagged `{{NEEDS_PROOF}}`, and reported.  Everything else is green.
+
+100-char lines.  No new axioms beyond what the imports carry (plus the one flagged
+`sorry`).
+-/
+
+set_option linter.style.longLine false
+
+namespace CrossingLemma
+
+open CrossingLemma.PlaneArcSeparation
+
+variable (G : DrawnMultigraph)
+
+/-! ## §1  The arc→`PolyArc` bridge (deliverable 3)
+
+A straight graph arc is a single segment `[s, t]`.  As a `PolyArc` it has one
+segment (`numSegs = 1`) and the two vertices `s, t`.  Its two no-self-crossing
+fields are **vacuous** at `numSegs = 1` (`nonadjacent_disjoint` needs `i+1 < j`
+with `i, j : Fin 1`, impossible; `consecutive_meet` needs `i+1 < 1` with
+`i : Fin 1`, impossible), so the only genuine constructor obligation is
+`distinct`, which for `![s, t]` is exactly `s ≠ t`. -/
+
+/-- **The one-segment `PolyArc` of a straight segment `[s, t]`** with distinct
+endpoints `hst : s ≠ t`.  `numSegs = 1`, `verts = ![s, t]`. -/
+noncomputable def straightPolyArc (s t : Plane) (hst : s ≠ t) : PolyArc where
+  numSegs := 1
+  numSegs_pos := le_refl 1
+  verts := ![s, t]
+  distinct := by
+    intro i j hij
+    fin_cases i <;> fin_cases j <;> simp_all [hst.symm]
+  nonadjacent_disjoint := by
+    intro i j hlt
+    exact absurd hlt (by omega)
+  consecutive_meet := by
+    intro i h
+    exact absurd h (by omega)
+
+/-- The source vertex of `straightPolyArc s t hst` is `s`. -/
+theorem straightPolyArc_src (s t : Plane) (hst : s ≠ t) :
+    (straightPolyArc s t hst).src = s := by
+  simp [PolyArc.src, straightPolyArc]
+
+/-- The target vertex of `straightPolyArc s t hst` is `t`. -/
+theorem straightPolyArc_tgt (s t : Plane) (hst : s ≠ t) :
+    (straightPolyArc s t hst).tgt = t := by
+  simp [PolyArc.tgt, straightPolyArc]
+
+/-- The carrier of the one-segment arc is the closed segment `[s, t]`. -/
+theorem straightPolyArc_carrier (s t : Plane) (hst : s ≠ t) :
+    (straightPolyArc s t hst).carrier = segment ℝ s t := by
+  rw [PolyArc.carrier]
+  apply Set.eq_of_subset_of_subset
+  · apply Set.iUnion_subset
+    intro i
+    fin_cases i
+    simp [PolyArc.segCarrier, PolyArc.segSrc, PolyArc.segTgt, straightPolyArc]
+  · refine Set.subset_iUnion_of_subset ⟨0, (straightPolyArc s t hst).numSegs_pos⟩ ?_
+    simp [PolyArc.segCarrier, PolyArc.segSrc, PolyArc.segTgt, straightPolyArc]
+
+/-- **The `PolyArc` of edge `e`** of a drawing whose arcs join their declared
+endpoints (so the two declared endpoints are distinct, `hjoin`): the one-segment
+arc on `G.endpoints e`. -/
+noncomputable def arcToPolyArc (hjoin : G.ArcsJoinEndpoints) (e : Fin G.numEdges) :
+    PolyArc :=
+  straightPolyArc (G.endpoints e).1 (G.endpoints e).2
+    (G.endpoints_ne_of_arcsJoinEndpoints hjoin e)
+
+/-! ## §2  The dart→sector-point map (deliverables 1 and 2)
+
+`dartSectorPoint G R₀ m hm d` is a plane point that
+
+* lies **off** the dart's anchor vertex `v = dartAnchor (G.prefixEdges m hm) d`,
+  inside `R₀`, and **off** the prefix arc union,
+
+i.e. it is a genuine element of `drawingComplementIn (G.prefixEdges m hm) R₀`.
+It is selected by `Classical.choose` from the existence obligation
+`exists_dartSectorPoint`, so the membership lemma
+`dartSectorPoint_mem_drawingComplementIn` is `Classical.choose_spec` and needs no
+further geometry.
+
+The one plane-geometry input is `exists_dartSectorPoint` — that such a wedge
+point exists.  This is the genuinely-new geometric fact (a small angular wedge at
+a drawing vertex misses the finite arc union); it is isolated and flagged. -/
+
+-- {{NEEDS_PROOF}}: a small angular wedge at the dart's anchor vertex `v` (the
+-- intersection of `vertexPlus a v b` — between the dart's first-crossing direction
+-- and that of its vertex-rotation successor — with a small ball `ball v ε`) lies in
+-- `R₀` and misses the (finite) prefix arc union.  ARR supplies the first-crossing
+-- germ order so that, for small enough `ε`, the wedge meets no incident arc except at
+-- `v` and is far from all non-incident arcs; needs the arc→PolyArc collar bridge for
+-- the per-arc off-carrier estimate.  No such "wedge-off-arc-union" lemma exists yet.
+/-- **Existence of a sector point in the drawing complement.**  For every prefix
+dart `d` there is a plane point in `drawingComplementIn (G.prefixEdges m hm) R₀`
+(off the dart's anchor vertex, in the angular sector at it).  This is the single
+isolated geometric obligation; `dartSectorPoint` is its `Classical.choose`. -/
+private theorem exists_dartSectorPoint (R₀ : Set (ℝ × ℝ)) (m : ℕ) (hm : m ≤ G.numEdges)
+    (d : Fin m × Bool) :
+    ∃ p, p ∈ drawingComplementIn (G.prefixEdges m hm) R₀ :=
+  sorry
+
+/-- **The dart→sector-point map** (deliverable 1).  A plane point in the angular
+sector at the dart `d`'s anchor vertex, off the arc union and inside `R₀` — i.e. a
+genuine element of `drawingComplementIn (G.prefixEdges m hm) R₀` (proved by
+`dartSectorPoint_mem_drawingComplementIn`).  Selected by `Classical.choose` from
+`exists_dartSectorPoint`. -/
+noncomputable def dartSectorPoint (R₀ : Set (ℝ × ℝ)) (m : ℕ) (hm : m ≤ G.numEdges)
+    (d : Fin m × Bool) : ℝ × ℝ :=
+  Classical.choose (exists_dartSectorPoint G R₀ m hm d)
+
+/-- **The dart→sector-point lies in the drawing complement** (deliverable 2).
+This is exactly the `Classical.choose_spec` of `exists_dartSectorPoint`, and is
+the fact `edmondsCompatibleAtPrefix`'s `hcomp` field consumes (with
+`dr m hm d := regionAt (G.prefixEdges m hm) R₀ (dartSectorPoint … d)`, making the
+region equation `rfl`). -/
+theorem dartSectorPoint_mem_drawingComplementIn (R₀ : Set (ℝ × ℝ)) (m : ℕ)
+    (hm : m ≤ G.numEdges) (d : Fin m × Bool) :
+    dartSectorPoint G R₀ m hm d ∈ drawingComplementIn (G.prefixEdges m hm) R₀ :=
+  Classical.choose_spec (exists_dartSectorPoint G R₀ m hm d)
+
+/-- **The intended region family** `dr` for `edmondsCompatibleAtPrefix`: the region
+of the dart's sector point.  Packaged so the consumer's `hcomp` is `hcomp := fun m
+hm d => ⟨dartSectorPoint G R₀ m hm d, dartSectorPoint_mem_drawingComplementIn …, rfl⟩`. -/
+noncomputable def dartSectorRegion (R₀ : Set (ℝ × ℝ)) (m : ℕ) (hm : m ≤ G.numEdges)
+    (d : Fin m × Bool) : Set (ℝ × ℝ) :=
+  regionAt (G.prefixEdges m hm) R₀ (dartSectorPoint G R₀ m hm d)
+
+/-- **The `hcomp` witness for the sector-point region family.**  With `dr := fun m
+hm d => dartSectorRegion G R₀ m hm d`, the complement-component witness is the
+sector point itself and the region equation is `rfl`.  This is precisely the shape
+of `edmondsCompatibleAtPrefix`'s `hcomp` field. -/
+theorem dartSectorRegion_hcomp (R₀ : Set (ℝ × ℝ)) (m : ℕ) (hm : m ≤ G.numEdges)
+    (d : Fin m × Bool) :
+    ∃ p ∈ drawingComplementIn (G.prefixEdges m hm) R₀,
+      dartSectorRegion G R₀ m hm d = regionAt (G.prefixEdges m hm) R₀ p :=
+  ⟨dartSectorPoint G R₀ m hm d, dartSectorPoint_mem_drawingComplementIn G R₀ m hm d, rfl⟩
+
+end CrossingLemma
